Simultaneous vs. Non-Simultaneous Calls: If function calls are not simultaneous, they do not stack up in memory. int pairSumSequence(int n) {
    int sum = 0;
    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
        sum += pairSum(i, i + 1);
    }
    return sum;
}
int pairSum(int a, int b) {
    return a + b;
}

